{
  "storyId": "B-06b3",
  "name": "experience-ab-shadow-gate",
  "title": "Experience Layer 3.3: deterministic A/B hintMode + shadow-gated experience-hint display",
  "description": "Assign every story a deterministic, pre-registered hintMode (on/off) and gate the advisory experience-hints SECTION so reviewers see it only in the ON arm, while hints are still COMPUTED and the experience_hint_surfaced event still fires (now carrying hintMode) on BOTH arms. This sets up a clean, unconfounded forward A/B: no story loses measurement (the would-have-hinted data is recorded for OFF too), only the ON arm gets the reviewer-facing nudge. Hints already live solely in the advisory _reviewPrompt channel (separate from resolveReviewPromptHash), so the gating never perturbs promptHash, the issues/blocker computation, or any gate.",
